# Line endings.
#
# Every text file in this repo is stored LF in the index and checked out LF in
# the working tree, on every platform. `eol=lf` is what makes the working-tree
# half of that true: without it, a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true`
# rewrites all 205 text files to CRLF on checkout, and `git status` then reports
# them as modified forever even though `git diff` is empty.
#
# LF is already what the index holds, so this file is a no-op on content —
# `git add --renormalize .` stages nothing. It pins the current state rather
# than changing it.
#
# The theme ships no build step, and its consumers are PHP, CSS, JS, and
# WordPress block markup, none of which care about EOL. The two .ps1 scripts run
# under PowerShell 5.1+, which reads LF scripts fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize EOL, never diff as text.
# Git already auto-detects all of these; declaring them keeps that from
# depending on content sniffing.
*.png   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.zip   binary
